# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quest 3 diagnostics -- what stays out of git, and why.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything a session writes lives under runs/<run_id>/: sampler TSVs, OVR CSV, VrApi logcat,
# results.json, and optionally a wire capture (cap.pcapng/cap.etl) or a WPR trace (GB per minute).
# It is local test data tied to one machine's AP/headset, not a portable measurement, so none of it
# ships -- and it was purged from history. Regenerate by re-running a session; a trace is read in WPA
# and the conclusions belong in the write-ups, not in the trace.
/runs/

# Machine-bound credentials: Virtual Desktop's DPAPI blobs (ProtectedComputerID,
# Accounts.OculusQuest) are user+machine scoped secrets. Never publish.
**/pc_config.json

# This rig's profile: real paths, IPs, SSIDs. Tracked template is site.example.json.
tools/site.json

# Harness runtime state (written while a cell runs).
tools/current_run_id.txt
tools/elev-cmd.txt
tools/elev-do-cmd.txt
tools/elev-res.txt
tools/elev-do-res.txt
tools/elev-setup-log.txt
tools/*.log

# Raw adb device dumps: regenerate with tools/Quest-Probe.ps1. They carry the
# headset serial/MACs and neighbors' SSIDs/BSSIDs from scan lists.
probe/**/raw/
probe/**/*-raw/

# Local agent write-up from a probe session, like handoff.md: dev-side notes rather than a published
# measurement (the probe's own SUMMARY.md/index.json stay tracked alongside the other probe dirs).
probe/2026-09-20-110528/agent-ethernet.md

# AP administration screenshot with the Wi-Fi passphrase rendered in plaintext.
topology/ap-radio.png

# Bug report written for external submission. Carries the reporter's name and contact address, which a
# public push would publish. Kept local on purpose -- it is still regenerable from the run artifacts
# (results.json + retry_rate_samples.tsv + pc_samples.tsv) if it ever needs to be rewritten.
docs/quest3-bt-wifi-coexistence-report.md

# Working handoff notes for whoever picks this up locally. Kept out of the repository so the published
# tree stays the tool plus its documented measurements, rather than a moving list of what is next.
handoff.md

# The author's own running write-ups and aggregate measurement table. Root-anchored on purpose: the
# same names inside runs/ (e.g. analyze.py's `report <runs_dir>` output) are separate, regenerable
# files. Purged from history too -- see the "Keep local write-ups out of the published tree" commit.
/findings.md
/report.md
/results.csv

# Third-party aarch64 Android build of iperf3 (BSD-3-Clause). Fetch or build your own.
tools/iperf3.*

# Third-party PresentMon console-app build (MIT). Fetch your own from
# https://github.com/GameTechDev/PresentMon/releases/latest and point presentmon_exe at it.
tools/vendor/

# The whole baseline/ tree is this rig's own local state, not a portable measurement: per-configuration
# fingerprint "current normal" (regenerate with `cell.py fingerprint <run_id> --save-baseline`) plus the
# manual iperf3/ping network baselines. Nothing here is committed, and it was purged from history too.
/baseline/

# Any run_id prefixed with "priv_" (e.g. priv_ram3600_...) is a personal sanity-check: `cell.py
# results`/`passive` skip its row in the local results.csv (see is_private_run() in tools/cell.py).
# The run directory itself needs no rule -- runs/ is ignored wholesale above.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Release build: scratch (downloaded platform-tools) and output (PyInstaller dist + zip). Both fully
# regenerable by `python release/build_release.py` -- see release/README.md.
release/build/
release/dist/
